<%- include('partials/head', { title: 'Reading' }) %>
<%- include('partials/spine', { nav: 'reading' }) %>

<main class="sheet" data-key="reading">
  <span class="crop tl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop tr" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop bl" aria-hidden="true"></span>
  <span class="crop br" aria-hidden="true"></span>

  <div class="block pt-20" id="block">

    <%- include('partials/desk', { deskQuery: '' }) %>

    <%# The section's own mark, as clubs carries one, so the page is
        identifiable before a word of it is read. %>
    <div class="press-kicker mono-s"><i aria-hidden="true"></i>READING — <%=
      books.length %> ON PRESS</div>
    <h1 class="d2 mb-30">On press</h1>

    <%#
      This page collapses to ONE interaction: say what page you are on.

      Everything that used to be here and is not any more:

      — FINISHED and ABANDON. Once-per-book decisions, near-irreversible, and
        they were sitting a mis-click away on a screen opened every morning.
        They live on the book page, where the decision is being made.
      — DUE. A deadline is exactly the pressure the footer promises this
        product does not apply. It survives only where it is a fact rather
        than a goal: a library loan, shown on the book that is borrowed.
      — The pace strip's empty state. A heading that announces its own
        emptiness is the "THE COLOPHON — UNKNOWN" failure again.
      — LOG IMPRESSION. A press impression is a lovely fit for "on press",
        and nobody would ever guess it meant "record my page". A number
        field that saves itself needs no verb at all.
    %>

    <% if (!books.length) { %>
      <%# B4 — zero active books is not an error state. An invitation, per §10. %>
      <p class="empty note note-lg">Nothing on press.</p>
      <a class="btn" href="/desk">FIND A BOOK</a>
    <% } %>

    <div class="press-rows">
    <% books.forEach(function(b) { %>
      <%
        var label = h.positionLabel(b.position_type);
        var value = b.current_page ? String(Math.round(b.current_page)) : '';
      %>
      <section class="press-row" data-work="<%= b.work_id %>">

        <a class="press-cover" href="/work/<%= b.work_id %>" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true">
          <%- h.frame(b) %>
        </a>

        <div class="press-body">
          <a class="press-title" href="/work/<%= b.work_id %>"><%= b.title %></a>

          <div class="press-meta mono-s dim">
            <%= b.authorLine %><%
              /* The extent belongs on the byline, where a catalogue puts it —
                 it is a fact about the edition, not about this reading. */
              if (b.totalPositions) { %> · <%= b.totalPositions %>PP<% }
              /* PASS 2 is a fact about the row, not an alarm. The accent was
                 landing here AND on the button beside it, so two reds were
                 competing in one row for a screen that is allowed one. */
              if (b.pass_number > 1) { %> · PASS <%= b.pass_number %><% } %>
          </div>

          <%#
            The gap, lifted out of the byline and given the weight it earns.

            How long a book has been sitting is the one fact on this row that
            might change what somebody does today, and it was set in 9pt mono
            between the author and everything else. It is now the second
            thing read. Warm only once the book has actually stalled — a
            number that shouts on day two is a number nobody believes on
            day thirty.
          %>
          <% if (b.daysSinceLog != null) { %>
            <div class="press-gap<%= b.stalled ? ' is-stale' : '' %>">
              <b><%= b.daysSinceLog %></b>
              <span class="mono-s">DAY<%= b.daysSinceLog === 1 ? '' : 'S' %> SINCE LAST LOGGED</span>
            </div>
          <% } else if (b.started_at) { %>
            <div class="press-gap">
              <span class="mono-s">STARTED TODAY</span>
            </div>
          <% } %>

          <%#
            The three endings, on the row.

            These lived on the book page for a while, on the argument that
            near-irreversible decisions should not sit a mis-click away on a
            screen opened every morning. The single link that replaced them
            could not say which of the three you were going to get, and a
            pass you want rid of took two screens to be rid of. They are
            back where the redesign puts them.

            They are POSTs, not links: each carries CSRF, each is a real
            form, and DISCARD carries the pass number so it cannot delete a
            later pass started in another tab. `discard` refuses server-side
            when a pass is the only record of having read something, so the
            control cannot destroy that even from here.
          %>
          <div class="press-acts">
            <form method="post" action="/work/<%= b.work_id %>/finish" class="inline-form">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
              <button class="press-act mono-s" type="submit">FINISHED</button>
            </form>
            <span class="press-act-sep mono-s" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
            <form method="post" action="/work/<%= b.work_id %>/abandon" class="inline-form">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
              <%# Where they stopped, so the stamp records a page rather than
                  a blank. %>
              <input type="hidden" name="page" value="<%= b.current_page || '' %>">
              <button class="press-act mono-s" type="submit">ABANDONED</button>
            </form>
            <span class="press-act-sep mono-s" aria-hidden="true">·</span>
            <form method="post" action="/work/<%= b.work_id %>/discard" class="inline-form">
              <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">
              <input type="hidden" name="pass" value="<%= b.pass_number %>">
              <button class="press-act press-act-quiet mono-s" type="submit">DISCARD THIS PASS</button>
            </form>
          </div>

          <% if (b.stalled) { %>
            <p class="press-stall mono-s dim">
              NO SESSION IN <%= b.daysSinceLog %> DAYS. ABANDONING IS FINE.
            </p>
          <% } %>

          <%#
            A due date appears only when the book is genuinely borrowed — a
            fact with a date attached, not a target somebody set for themselves.
          %>
          <% if (b.due_date) { %>
            <p class="press-due mono-s <%= b.dueSoon ? 'accent' : 'dim' %>">
              DUE <%= h.monthDay(b.due_date) %><%
                if (b.daysUntilDue < 0) { %> · <%= Math.abs(b.daysUntilDue) %> DAYS OVER<% } %>
            </p>
          <% } %>
        </div>

        <%#
          The page number IS the input. Click it, type, blur saves. No verb,
          no label, no box — the number sits where a number would sit on a
          running sheet, and the extent beside it behaves the same way.

          A book the catalogue has no page count for has no ceiling, no
          percentage and no mark on the rule, and the reader is the only one
          who can say how long the object in their hands is. Set it once and
          it bounds every log after.
        %>
        <form class="press-count" method="post" action="/work/<%= b.work_id %>/log">
          <input type="hidden" name="_csrf" value="<%= csrfToken %>">

          <div class="press-figure">
            <input class="press-number"
                   name="position"
                   type="text"
                   inputmode="numeric"
                   autocomplete="off"
                   value="<%= value %>"
                   data-value="<%= value %>"
                   data-total="<%= b.totalPositions || '' %>"
                   placeholder="—"
                   aria-label="<%= label %> in <%= b.title %>">
            <span class="press-of mono-s dim">/</span>
            <input class="press-extent mono-s"
                   name="total"
                   type="text"
                   inputmode="numeric"
                   autocomplete="off"
                   value="<%= b.totalPositions || '' %>"
                   data-value="<%= b.totalPositions || '' %>"
                   data-extent-post="/work/<%= b.work_id %>/extent"
                   placeholder="?"
                   aria-label="Total <%= label.toLowerCase() %>s in <%= b.title %>">
          </div>

          <div class="press-unit mono-s dim"><%= label %></div>

          <%#
            One hairline with a red mark — the same treatment the home screen
            uses, so the same idiom means the same thing in both places. Not
            a filled bar: a fill is a score, and a mark is just where you are.

            A book with no extent gets a broken rule rather than a solid one,
            because there is no line to be somewhere along yet.
          %>
          <div class="press-track<%= b.totalPositions ? '' : ' is-unknown' %>"<%
               if (b.percent) { %> role="img" aria-label="<%= b.percent %> percent"<% } %>>
            <% if (b.percent) { %>
              <i class="press-mark"
                 id="<%= h.rule(styleRules, 'pm', b.work_id, 'left:' + h.css.pct(b.percent)) %>"></i>
            <% } %>
          </div>

          <div class="press-pct mono-s dim">
            <%= b.totalPositions ? (b.percent || 0) + ' PER CENT' : 'LENGTH UNKNOWN' %>
          </div>

          <%#
            Plain mono text, no boxes, and only on the row you are in. They
            are submit buttons so the page still works with no JavaScript;
            the styling is what makes them read as text.
          %>
          <div class="press-adds">
            <% [10, 25, 50].forEach(function(n) { %>
              <button class="press-add mono-s" type="submit" name="advance" value="<%= n %>"
                      tabindex="-1">+<%= n %></button>
            <% }) %>
          </div>

          <%# Without JavaScript, Enter submits and this is the fallback. %>
          <noscript><button class="press-add mono-s" type="submit">SAVE</button></noscript>
        </form>
      </section>
    <% }) %>
    </div>

  </div>

<%- include('partials/foot') %>
